## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical knowledge of observability in a beginner Azure stack, ensuring the candidate can wire instrumentation, telemetry exports, and basic dashboards end-to-end.

## Key Concepts
- OpenTelemetry integration in Azure Functions
- Application Insights exporter and per-endpoint metrics
- Sampling, traces, and dashboards in Azure Monitor
- GitHub Actions CI/CD for deployments
- Front Door TLS endpoint configuration
- SQL Auto Failover Group for cross-region DR

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal OpenTelemetry setup (Node.js)
const { NodeSDK } = require('@opentelemetry/sdk-node');
const { getNodeAutoInstrumentations } = require('@opentelemetry/auto-instrumentations-node');
const { AzureMonitorTraceExporter } = require('@opentelemetry/exporter-azure-monitor');

const sdk = new NodeSDK({
  traceExporter: new AzureMonitorTraceExporter({
    connectionString: process.env.APPLICATIONINSIGHTS_CONNECTION_STRING
  }),
  instrumentations: [getNodeAutoInstrumentations()],
  sampler: new AlwaysParentSampler(0.2) // 20% sampling
});

sdk.start();
```

## Why This Is Asked
Introduces App Configuration feature flags and per-user gating in a beginner stack, testing security, governance, and DR awareness.

## Key Concepts
- Azure Static Web Apps
- Azure Functions (Consumption)
- Azure App Configuration (flags)
- Azure Front Door (TLS)
- Entra ID with group-based access
- GitHub Actions CI/CD
- Cross-region DR (App Configuration and SQL)

## Code Example
```javascript
// Azure Function (Node.js) reading a flag from App Configuration
const { AppConfigurationClient } = require("@azure/app-configuration");
module.exports = async function (context, req) {
  const client = new AppConfigurationClient(process.env.APPCFG_ENDPOINT);
  const setting = await client.getConfigurationSetting({ key: "flags:newChat" });
  context.res = { body: { enableChat: setting.value === "true" } };
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you ensure the frontend never exposes secret keys while consuming App Configuration flags?
- What are the trade-offs of geo-replication for App Configuration and SQL in this scenario?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design multi-tenant real-time analytics on Azure with data isolation, security, DR, governance, and CI/CD. Combines streaming, storage, analytics, API security, and cross-region considerations.

## Key Concepts

- Event Hubs, Durable Functions, Function Apps
- Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2, Synapse, Row-Level Security
- API Management, Azure Entra ID, per-tenant RBAC
- Private Link for back-end service access
- Azure Policy, Cost Management budgets
- Cross-region DR, event replay, API failover

## Code Example

```javascript
// Skeleton: orchestration with per-tenant workflow (pseudo)
import { orchestrator } from 'durable-functions';
export const runFraudWorkflow = orchestrator(function*(context) {
  const event = context.bindings.input;
  yield context.df.callActivity('ValidateEvent', event);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would onboarding/offboarding tenants affect RBAC and data isolation?
- How would you test end-to-end DR failover and event replay scenarios?
